---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Astrum Invictum | Syntheion Dynamics"
  description="Transmedia sci-fi about rebuilding civilization after collapse through Matter, Mind, and Steel."
  mode="studio"
  sector="Astrum Invictum"
  ogImage="/images/mini-astrum-landscape.jpg"
>
  <Hero
    title="Astrum Invictum"
    subtitle="Unity demo in active development. A post-collapse civilization rebuilt through Matter, Mind, and Steel."
    image="/images/mini-astrum-landscape.jpg"
    ctaHref="https://astruminvictum.com"
    ctaLabel="Open astruminvictum.com"
  />

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Project" title="Science, governance, and presence" />
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <div>
        <p>
          Astrum Invictum is a transmedia sci-fi project about rebuilding civilization after collapse. The setting is
          Vindex Caelum, a ringworld where law, systems engineering, and psionic research evolve together instead of
          competing for control.
        </p>
        <p>
          After the Great Catastrophe, the maintenance AI Echo activated dormant archives and initiated genetic
          restoration of ten races. Under Empress Velia Serapha and Lucia's research leadership, the empire stabilizes
          around three pillars: Matter, Mind, and Steel.
        </p>
        <p>
          In this universe, faith is not about gods. It is disciplined trust in causality, in responsibility, and in
          the fact that consciousness is part of the universe, not separate from it. Science defines what is possible.
          Presence defines how power is used.
        </p>
        <p><a class="button" href="https://astruminvictum.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Go to main Astrum site</a></p>
      </div>
      <img class="enlargeable" src="/images/mini-astrum-statue-fp.jpg" alt="Astrum Invictum first person statue scene" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VINDEX CAELUM -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Setting" title="Vindex Caelum" subtitle="The ringworld at the center of the story." />
    <img
      class="enlargeable wide-image"
      src="/images/mini-astrum-vindex-closeup.jpg"
      alt="Vindex Caelum ringworld closeup concept art"
    />
    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      Vindex Caelum is an ancient megastructure — a ringworld of unknown origin. Its districts range from classical
      civic architecture to industrial sectors and frontier zones at the edges. The empire's legal system is
      decentralized by design, adapted to the scale and diversity of the ring. Three district types, three sets of
      laws, one supreme tribunal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- TRIUMVIRATE -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Leadership" title="The Triumvirate" />
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[AI ECHO]</p>
        <p>
          Former maintenance AI, now the empire's continuity authority and archival intelligence. Echo initiated
          civilization's restoration from genetic fragments after 800 years of hibernation. Her current mandate
          prioritizes collective coherence over individual doubt — by necessity, not preference.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[EMPRESS VELIA SERAPHA]</p>
        <p>
          Raised by Echo personally, Velia Serapha holds the empire together through a combination of political
          pragmatism and public legitimacy. Her proclamation of the First Light elevated governance into a framework
          that citizens can believe in, not just obey.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[LUCIA — HEAD OF RESEARCH]</p>
        <p>
          Lucia does not calculate equations — she perceives them. Her intuitive access to Hexaterion field structures
          makes her the empire's most critical scientific asset and its main defense against dimensional
          destabilization.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FLEET DOCTRINE -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Doctrine" title="Operational duality: force and guidance" />
    <div class="grid-2">
      <img class="enlargeable" src="/images/mini-astrum-ships-via-ignis-lyra.jpg" alt="SCE Via Ignis and USS Lyra Accord" />
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[FLEET LOGIC]</p>
        <p>
          <strong>SCE Via Ignis</strong> is force projection. Built inside Hexaterion with a hull density approaching
          that of a neutron star, it is a reality icebreaker — but blind in the dimensional space it operates in.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>USS Lyra Accord</strong> carries no weapons. Its sensor arrays perceive dimensional currents that no
          other instrument can read. It navigates the Sword.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">One without the other does not survive Hexaterion. That dependency is also the doctrine.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HEXATERION TEASER -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader
      sector="Metaphysics"
      title="Hexaterion"
      subtitle="Six-vector dimensional space where standard physics does not apply."
    />
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Hexaterion is not a place. It is a topological structure where reality operates on six independent axes:
        Temporal, Metric, Mass, Polarity, Information, and Causal. The speed of light is not a limit here — it is the
        minimum condition for coherence. Anything slower disintegrates into information noise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Psionic operators navigate this space through trained resonance rather than instrumentation. The risk is not
        equipment failure. The risk is identity dissolution.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Full mechanics documented on astruminvictum.com</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CULTURAL ARCHIVE -->
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader
      sector="Cultural Archive"
      title="Civilian life and identity artifacts"
      subtitle="The empire is also advertising agencies, sports events, and housing brands."
    />
    <div class="grid-2">
      <img class="enlargeable" src="/images/mini-astrum-poster-domelux.jpg" alt="Domelux housing brand poster from Astrum Invictum" />
      <img
        class="enlargeable"
        src="/images/mini-astrum-poster-tour-de-promenade.jpg"
        alt="Tour de Promenade cycling event poster from Vindex Caelum"
      />
    </div>
    <blockquote>
      "We do not expand to dominate. We build so collapse does not repeat."
    </blockquote>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }

  .wide-image {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 480px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  blockquote {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .intro-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
